  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BBSRC strategic funding to eight institutes for ODA activities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BBSRC provides strategic funding to eight independent UK research institutes. They deliver innovative, world-class bioscience research and training. They have strong links with business, industry and the wider community, and support policy development in the UK and overseas. Please note: The grants included for institute programmes have been internally screened for ODA relevance. From financial year 2021-2022 elements of this funding have been identified as ODA which focus on: livestock and zoonotic diseases prevalent in developing countries; drug resistance in African livestock trypanosomes; plant parasites and adaptation of crops grown in LMICs to fungal pathogens; water use and pest management in LMICs; African swine fever, Rift Valley Fever and Avian influenza, which are endemic only in LMICs; selecting wheat for traits for LMIC conditions; and eradication of goat plague (PPR endemic in Asia, Middle East and Africa).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and development activity contributing to the UK&#x2019;s strategy to address key development challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
